# Space (live server): sp_combat cut after the kill, then two Next Target presses (brief CS4, 2026-11-26). The steps
# up to the kill's shot are sp_combat's (keep them in step: the mob's death point, and so the first press's pick,
# follows the fight). N (control_keys.ini [Next Target]) twice, each until the client asks (REQUEST_TARGET) and the
# server answers with the target's verbs (VERB_UPDATE: 0x18 bytes with the hulk's Loot verb, 0x10 with none, our
# own ship), a shot of the target window after each. Which object the first press picks is the client's sorted
# list (target_find.cpp Build_List 0x7C4530: every targetable object by sphere distance 0x7E6130, the gap between
# the two spheres, 0 when they touch; std::sort 0x7C4E30): our own ship is always at 0, the hulk at 0 only when its
# centre lies within the two radii of ours, and then first by the object list's order (a new hash bucket's node goes
# to the list's head, wwlib hashlist.h Add). So the first press picks the hulk when the mob died close to us and our
# ship ('Admiral Elanor' in the target window) when it died farther out (CS4, 37 runs of sp_combat and this, 21
# retail, 16 ours: the hulk first at a centre distance of 74-216, our ship first at 220-247, both clients alike;
# mob_destroyed's draw log gives the distance: the new model position with the most vertices). No loot is taken: the
# hulk is left to the server, whose state the next run's restart and --db-snapshot restore.
# Run: e2e.py --live --retail --db-snapshot 7 --instance space run sp_nexttarget (it changes Elanor's hull).
name: space combat cut after the kill: two Next Target presses, the first press's pick and the hulk's distance
timeout: 360
include _login_space
# the GM command in the chat entry; the server answers 'Creating Renegade Progen Tribuni at level 45' and creates it
key 0x0D
wait-quiet proxy 0.5 within 10
text '/createmob 1993'
key 0x0D
expect-event antprox 'received CLIENT_CHAT$' within 10
wait-event antprox 'sent CREATE$' within 15
wait-event antprox 'sent RELATIONSHIP$' within 15
shot mob_created
# E again until the client asks: right after the CREATE it may not yet know the mob (run 231808 sent nothing)
key 0x45 until antprox 'received REQUEST_TARGET$' every 1.5 within 20
wait-event antprox 'sent SET_TARGET$' within 10
shot mob_targeted
# the hotbar as the client data's shortcut.ini (ClientPOC's, copied afresh into every instance) has it, clicked as the
# recording clicked its slot: 1-3 three weapons, slot 4 Biocessation (organic targets only), slot 5 Enrage Group, 6
# another skill. The recording's slot 4 Rally and slot 5 Repair Equipment are not there: waiting for an
# OBJECT_EFFECT after slot 4 failed on retail every time (2026-11-25: the server answers the Progen target with a
# PRIORITY_MESSAGE, the client's message line, and no effect; sp_warp's slot 5 is answered so too). Each click is
# repeated until the client sends SKILL_ABILITY (store .staging run 005451: one click 0.2 s after SET_TARGET sent
# nothing), then the server's answer, an effect or the message, is waited for
click 790,960 until antprox 'received SKILL_ABILITY$' every 2 within 12
wait-event antprox 'sent (OBJECT_EFFECT|PRIORITY_MESSAGE)$' within 15
# the shot 1 s after the answer (2026-11-25 CS: shot at once, ours drew the PRIORITY_MESSAGE's text a frame later)
wait-since antprox 'sent (OBJECT_EFFECT|PRIORITY_MESSAGE)$' 1
shot skill_slot4
click 865,960 until antprox 'received SKILL_ABILITY$' every 2 within 12
wait-event antprox 'sent (OBJECT_EFFECT|PRIORITY_MESSAGE)$' within 15
wait-since antprox 'sent (OBJECT_EFFECT|PRIORITY_MESSAGE)$' 1
shot skill_slot5
# the effects (brief CS2, c4): Rally and Repair Equipment from the PDA, as the recording dragged Hacking. The PDA
# (the second button at the lower left), its Skills page, the list's down arrow until its end (30 clicks; Elanor's
# 19 skills end Reactor Tech, Repair Equipment, Shield Tech, Terran Culture), then its up arrow once: Rally on top
# (its first ability, rank 1, at 50,632), Repair Equipment third (its first at 50,785) (CS2 probe 2026-11-25: the
# list keeps no fixed start, but its end is fixed). A click on an ability there uses nothing (the probe: no
# SKILL_ABILITY); a drag onto the hotbar's slots 4 and 5 puts them there (the instance's shortcut.ini, a fresh copy
# each run). The server answers both with an OBJECT_EFFECT on our ship (Net-7 ARally: the buff's effect 333;
# ARepairEquipment: 170, a mob target defaults to self)
click 96,918
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 20
click 71,258
wait-quiet proxy 0.5 within 20
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,805
click 322,593
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 20
shot pda_skills
down 50,632
up 790,960
wait-quiet proxy 0.5 within 10
down 50,785
up 865,960
wait-quiet proxy 0.5 within 10
shot pda_dragged
click 322,258
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 20
click 790,960 until antprox 'received SKILL_ABILITY$' every 2 within 20
wait-event antprox 'sent OBJECT_EFFECT$' within 15
wait-since antprox 'sent OBJECT_EFFECT$' 1
shot skill_rally
click 865,960 until antprox 'received SKILL_ABILITY$' every 2 within 20
wait-event antprox 'sent OBJECT_EFFECT$' within 15
wait-since antprox 'sent OBJECT_EFFECT$' 1
shot skill_repair
key 0x46
expect-event antprox 'received ACTION$' within 10
wait-event antprox 'sent CLIENT_DAMAGE$' within 30
shot fighting
wait-event antprox 'sent POINT_EFFECT$' within 180
wait-event antprox 'sent CREATE$' within 15
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 30
shot mob_destroyed
# the first press: the client sends REQUEST_TARGET at once (sp_combat's runs: 0.04-0.07 s after the key); the
# server's SET_TARGET and VERB_UPDATE follow; the shot 1 s after the verbs (the target window's name and range)
key 0x4E until antprox 'received REQUEST_TARGET$' every 2 within 10
wait-event antprox 'sent VERB_UPDATE$' within 10
wait-since antprox 'sent VERB_UPDATE$' 1
shot next_target_1
key 0x4E until antprox 'received REQUEST_TARGET$' every 2 within 10
wait-event antprox 'sent VERB_UPDATE$' within 10
wait-since antprox 'sent VERB_UPDATE$' 1
shot next_target_2
expect-no CRASH
